  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Dakota received $497M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 2,823 awards with an average award size of $176K, and obligations fell 38.2% year over year. Federal buying in South Dakota has varied across recent fiscal years: FY21 totaled $624M, FY22 totaled $1.2B, FY23 totaled $1B, FY24 totaled $1.3B, and FY25 totaled $804M. The Department of Defense obligated $199M, making it the largest buyer in the state for FY2026 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $96.6M in obligations, followed by Computer Facilities Management Services at $68M. KBR WYLE SERVICES, LLC received $67.7M, the largest vendor total. Other significant agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services with $105M and the Department of the Interior with $91.8M. This snapshot covers partial current-year totals and focuses on contract obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers in South Dakota this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $199M and is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $105M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $91.8M. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $56.7M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $14.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors and industries lead federal spending in South Dakota?",
        "body": "KBR WYLE SERVICES, LLC received $67.7M and is the top vendor for FY2026 to date. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction led industries with $96.6M, followed by Computer Facilities Management Services with $68M. Other notable vendors include FEDERAL CONTRACTING INC with $40.4M and BLACK HILLS SERVICE COMPANY, LLC with $32.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
